AAA configuration in FRR (Forwarding and Routing Router) is managed via the `frr.conf` file under the `[daemons]` section, with authentication policies defined in the `[tacacs+]` or `[radius]` subsections, where server details (host, port, key, and shared secret) are specified alongside global AAA settings like default authentication methods and timeout values.

For TACACS+ integration, use:
```ini
[daemons]
zebra {
    ...
    aaa {
        tacacs+ {
            server 192.168.1.1 {
                key "shared-secret";
                port 49;
                timeout 5;
            }
            default {
                authentication {
                    method tacacs+;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
For RADIUS, replace the `[tacacs+]` block with:
```ini
[radius]
server 192.168.1.1 {
    key "shared-secret";
    port 1812;
    timeout 5;
}
```
Restart FRR (`systemctl restart frr`) or reload the daemon (`frr reload`) to apply changes.

