The `ietf-system` YANG model (RFC 6991) defines common operational data for system-level attributes such as **system uptime, boot time, hardware inventory (CPU, memory, disk), and operational state** (e.g., `system-state` with `running`, `stopped`, or `unknown` values), along with **system configuration status** (e.g., `config-commit-status` for pending changes) and **system performance metrics** (e.g., `system-cpu-usage` and `system-memory-usage` via `ietf-sensors` extensions).

Key operational data includes:
- **`system-uptime`** (duration since last reboot, in seconds)
- **`system-boot-time`** (timestamp of last boot)
- **`system-state`** (current operational state, e.g., `running`)
- **`system-config`** (current configuration state, including `config-commit-status` for pending changes)
- **`system-hardware`** (CPU, memory, and disk information via `ietf-sensors` or `ietf-sysinfo` extensions)
- **`system-performance`** (CPU/memory usage via `ietf-sensors` or `ietf-sysinfo` extensions).

Example YANG snippet for operational state:
```yang
module ietf-system {
  namespace "urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-system";
  prefix sys;

  container system {
    leaf uptime {
      type uint64;
      description "System uptime in seconds.";
    }
    leaf boot-time {
      type date-and-time;
      description "Timestamp of last boot.";
    }
    leaf state {
      type identityref {
        base sys:system-state-type;
      }
      description "Current system operational state.";
    }
    container config {
      leaf commit-status {
        type sys:config-commit-status-type;
        description "Status of pending configuration changes.";
      }
    }
  }
}
```

