```http
PATCH /nssai/{sst-sd}/slices/{slice-id}/slice-configuration
Headers:
  Content-Type: application/json
Body:
{
  "slice-configuration": {
    "slice-differentiator": {
      "sst": 9,  // Slice Service Type (e.g., 9 for URLLC)
      "sd": 1    // Slice Differentiator (custom per operator)
    },
    "slice-description": "Emergency-Vehicle-Urgent-Comms-Europe-Central",
    "qos-profile": {
      "qos-characteristics": {
        "priority-level": 15,  // Highest priority (0-15)
        "pre-emption-capability": "preemptable",
        "pre-emption-vulnerability": "preemptable",
        "fiveqi": 99,          // 5QI 99 (or equivalent for 99.999% reliability)
        "allocation-retention-priority": {
          "priority-level": 15,
          "pre-emption-capability": "preemptable",
          "pre-emption-vulnerability": "preemptable"
        }
      }
    },
    "reliability": {
      "target-reliability": 99.999,  // Explicit 5 nines reliability
      "mechanisms": [
        "ran-redundancy",
        "core-redundancy",
        "srvcc-fallback",
        "dual-connectivity"
      ]
    },
    "region": "Europe-Central",
    "emergency-services": true
  }
}
```
**Key Technical Notes:**
- **5QI 99** (or equivalent) must be mapped to **PFCP QoS rules** with **low packet loss (<0.001%)** and **jitter <1ms**.
